  ('3668774a-03d0-5384-b3e7-2d7def67a5d0', 'c1be6404-2a36-51f7-8d0f-43b1a6d26250', 5, 'Practice', 'practice', 'draft')
insert into public.tips (id, unit_id, title_en, body_md, status) values
  ('60d9b6af-f96e-577e-8d70-507d93bd9e91', '8a547039-7fc7-5382-9c3a-9b48a4102289', 'Me pidió que…', 'A request told later takes the past subjunctive: «Traeme pan» → **me pidió que le trajera pan**; «Esperen» → **nos dijo que esperáramos**. *Dijo que* + subjunctive is an order; *dijo que* + indicative is news.', 'draft'),
  ('31e9d7c0-8868-567b-a709-775f9c735a92', '8a547039-7fc7-5382-9c3a-9b48a4102289', 'Insistió, sugirió', '**Insistió en que fuera** — *she insisted I go*. **Me sugirió que la llamara** — *he suggested I call her*. Same pattern: the verb after **que** in the past subjunctive.', 'draft'),
  ('62b238a7-3a23-5bd2-a360-03b826c32105', 'd8c13ac1-8ec0-5db3-adbe-39834eed0ff9', 'Si = whether', 'A yes-or-no question told later hangs on **si**: «¿Venís?» → **me preguntó si venía**. *No sé si abre hoy* — *I don''t know if it''s open today*. **Dudo** — *I doubt it*.', 'draft'),
  ('ec1122a7-6b09-5324-b5c9-305542cf61e1', 'd8c13ac1-8ec0-5db3-adbe-39834eed0ff9', 'A ver si…', '**A ver si** is *let''s see if* — and, just as often, a hope: **a ver si nos juntamos** — *we should get together sometime*. To find something out, porteños **averiguan**.', 'draft'),
  ('dda7b964-bb56-5e48-bc13-d19abd0fc766', 'f71fcde3-a7e0-5429-864a-cef0a28a9a3f', 'Usted', 'Porteños say **vos** to almost everyone, but **usted** to an older stranger, a doctor, a building''s owner. Usted takes the *él* form of the verb: **¿usted es el dueño?**, **pase**, **siéntese**.', 'draft'),
  ('1d87549c-7542-53ad-8a97-9ed8aef021a6', 'f71fcde3-a7e0-5429-864a-cef0a28a9a3f', 'Quisiera', 'The politest way to ask is **quisiera** — *I''d like*: **quisiera un turno**. **Disculpe** gets attention, **le agradezco** says thank you. To a friend: **disculpá**, **te agradezco**.', 'draft'),
  ('533b1855-56b9-53e2-9459-caa67e63e95b', 'da717e1e-25b4-54db-a4c6-524cdb07bcfe', 'Me pidió que, me preguntó si', 'A request told later: **me pidió que le trajera algo**. A question: **me preguntó si venía**.', 'draft'),
  ('91a09edc-d241-50cf-8f47-268ab52bfee5', 'da717e1e-25b4-54db-a4c6-524cdb07bcfe', 'Usted', '**Disculpe**, **pase**, **siéntese**, **quisiera** — the *él* form, for someone you don''t tutear… or vosear.', 'draft'),
  ('e06c9bfd-3dd2-5980-a26d-595cd6ecb929', '68a6baaa-9e78-5479-aa65-63d51bc89b74', 'Estimado…', 'A work email opens with **Estimado Juan** or **Estimada Sofi** and ends with **Saludos**. **Te adjunto** is *I''m attaching*; **desde ya, gracias** is *thanks in advance*.', 'draft'),
  ('18cdbaf0-af94-565c-b117-e443aa6c4b17', '68a6baaa-9e78-5479-aa65-63d51bc89b74', 'Cualquier cosa, avisame', 'The porteño sign-off, in emails and out of them: **cualquier cosa, avisame** — *if anything comes up, let me know*. A **consulta** is a question you send; a **respuesta**, the reply.', 'draft'),
  ('b09d13bc-f73f-5448-80bf-e1a0406e6cf9', '9236841b-51b6-5a51-a400-9cf40915ec4e', 'Resulta que', '**Resulta que** — *it turns out* — is how a porteño story takes its turn. **Encima** — *on top of that* — makes it worse: **encima, llovía**. **Total** shrugs it off: **total, nadie se dio cuenta**.', 'draft'),
  ('19346301-1a24-55d3-b561-3583e04ce4c7', '9236841b-51b6-5a51-a400-9cf40915ec4e', 'Me enteré', '**Enterarse** is *to find out, to hear about*: **me enteré ayer**, **¿te enteraste?**, **se enteró todo el mundo**.', 'draft'),
  ('24f0169c-f457-5099-922f-4a497b84e8df', 'c64cedd2-5987-5859-b94d-77231e8c5eaa', 'Se la cree', 'A little **la** that points at nothing turns a verb into an idiom: **se la cree** — *he''s full of himself*; **me la banco** — *I can handle it*; **la tenés clara** — *you know your stuff*. With **las**: **me las arreglo** — *I get by*.', 'draft'),
  ('1fe7afdb-ae33-50c8-a0f2-fc35c6c6ac79', 'c64cedd2-5987-5859-b94d-77231e8c5eaa', 'La verdad', '**La verdad** opens an honest answer: **la verdad, no sé** — *honestly, I don''t know*. **La verdad que sí** — *yeah, really*.', 'draft'),
  ('d1e06ff5-4048-5e50-818b-97cd025a4f74', '94eb1988-d122-5fbd-be20-4599d41df698', 'Resulta que, encima', '**Resulta que** turns the story, **encima** makes it worse, **total** shrugs.', 'draft'),
  ('f8f1dd38-6b20-5a33-9fa8-3f6dc3e87775', '94eb1988-d122-5fbd-be20-4599d41df698', 'Se la cree, me la banco', '**Se la cree**, **me la banco**, **me las arreglo**, **la tenés clara** — a *la* that points at nothing.', 'draft'),
  ('043bf160-0648-51c6-bec2-2b7afbcb4c4a', '17f201ba-038f-5447-a92b-ea8274de3421', 'Acabo de', '**Acabo de** + infinitive is *I just did it*: **acabo de llegar**, **acaba de salir**. **Volví a** is *I did it again*: **volví a perder las llaves**. Or just **de nuevo**.', 'draft'),
  ('d578e8dc-eaae-5236-b408-a7b053f9755a', '17f201ba-038f-5447-a92b-ea8274de3421', 'Suelo', '**Soler** is *to usually*: **suelo almorzar tarde** — *I usually have lunch late*; **¿solés venir acá?** It only ever comes with an infinitive.', 'draft'),
  ('29090f79-278c-5890-bf3e-c89cc7947b4a', 'b27a8863-2d09-52bd-992f-2a73710c019d', 'Ya no', '**Ya no** is *not anymore*: **ya no vivo ahí**. **Cada vez más** — *more and more*: **cada vez más caro**; **cada vez menos** — *less and less*.', 'draft'),
  ('3b867a4a-8a39-52fc-bdb4-73a4c0c46453', 'b27a8863-2d09-52bd-992f-2a73710c019d', 'Creció', '**Crecer** is *to grow* — a city, a kid, a tree: **el barrio creció**, **crecí en Rosario** — *I grew up in Rosario*. The new towers are **edificios**.', 'draft'),
  ('aba5baad-8a36-5ee9-8293-ce942fa3dc14', 'f89dd37e-bd2f-5d8b-baac-6f770fe4838c', 'Harto, podrido', '**Estoy harto** — *I''m fed up*; porteños go further: **estoy podrido** — literally *rotten*. Both take **de**: **harta del tránsito**, **podrido del ruido**.', 'draft'),
  ('833b4252-9d5d-507e-8a20-d34d943f3bb8', 'f89dd37e-bd2f-5d8b-baac-6f770fe4838c', 'No doy más', '**No doy más** — *I can''t take it anymore*. **No lo aguanto** — *I can''t stand him*. And when it''s one thing too many: **¡es el colmo!**', 'draft'),
  ('36df2266-fe0a-5906-b980-3080e04096d3', '3c841aec-551f-5e12-a246-f16e72a12923', 'Acabo de, suelo, volví a', '**Acabo de** — just now; **suelo** — usually; **volví a** — again.', 'draft'),
  ('bd4af0ab-226e-57d8-a274-71896b65f5d6', '3c841aec-551f-5e12-a246-f16e72a12923', 'Ya no, cada vez más', '**Ya no** — not anymore; **cada vez más** — more and more. And when it''s too much: **estoy podrido**.', 'draft'),
  ('534e2bd7-f308-543e-af35-642336a8e744', '05427875-acf1-52fc-b7b9-15150a0edca2', 'Te la hago corta', '**Te la hago corta** — *long story short* — is usually followed by a long story. **La cuestión es que** — *the thing is* — brings it back on track; **en fin** closes it.', 'draft'),
  ('6fd250c0-fa1b-50b6-b892-4e0ec3d17d95', '05427875-acf1-52fc-b7b9-15150a0edca2', 'Y nada', '**Y nada** is the porteño *so, yeah*: it fills the pause at the end of a story. **Al toque** — *right away*: **me contestó al toque**.', 'draft'),
  ('0c7552f3-e3f0-58fe-a0e2-9b920941566b', '4619994d-18cb-57a3-aa86-ef5fd9551f1b', 'Hay paro', 'A strike is a **paro**: **hay paro de subte**, **paro de colectivos**. When protesters block a street it''s a **piquete** or a **corte**, and the street **está cortada**. A **marcha** is a march.', 'draft'),
  ('6ce81526-2ff0-5977-9bbf-fd1e8d406e0b', '4619994d-18cb-57a3-aa86-ef5fd9551f1b', 'No funciona', '**Funcionar** is *to work* for things: **el subte no funciona**, **los semáforos no funcionan**. For people, it''s still *laburar*.', 'draft'),
  ('d72e949d-a21c-57a2-b59e-58aec03fc440', 'f46f9df0-afdf-5c8c-95be-a4b002904a9d', 'Fue construido', 'The news likes the passive: **fue** + participle. **El puente fue construido en 1900**; **la estación fue inaugurada ayer**. The participle agrees like an adjective: *construido, construida*.', 'draft'),
  ('5f88a88d-8066-58cb-99c8-edeb9d5d9112', 'f46f9df0-afdf-5c8c-95be-a4b002904a9d', 'Fueron detenidos', 'More than one: **fueron detenidos** — *they were arrested*. In conversation porteños turn it around: *construyeron el puente*, *los detuvieron*.', 'draft'),
  ('67c1e923-9983-5e50-a6ce-52ff85a6eb09', '38d68ef5-9223-5ff2-8954-88f3a9cc0ef3', 'Votar', 'In Argentina voting is **obligatorio**. **¿A quién votaste?** is a real question, though many answer **eso no se pregunta**. **Votar a** someone: *voté a la misma candidata*.', 'draft'),
  ('eac6d092-ac6a-51cb-ad45-36a8a79f1e96', '38d68ef5-9223-5ff2-8954-88f3a9cc0ef3', 'Las elecciones', '**Las elecciones** — *the elections* — decide the **gobierno** and the **presidente**. The course stays out of it: the words, not the opinions.', 'draft'),
  ('b76db757-790f-5e97-9bd8-0076c09777a6', '7743587b-284d-5f25-8f96-38e8f9443429', 'Hay paro', '**Paro**, **corte**, **piquete** — and the street **está cortada**.', 'draft'),
  ('2f3509d9-ba13-5afe-9c07-b5a7cbea5e59', '7743587b-284d-5f25-8f96-38e8f9443429', 'Fue construido', '**Fue** + participle, agreeing: **fue construido**, **fue inaugurada**, **fueron detenidos**.', 'draft'),
  ('5c404af7-97bb-5016-95f3-4dbb7f00df17', 'd7836b8d-78b8-51ae-8e41-57e6f2d5de34', 'Según', '**Según** — *according to*: **según el diario**, **según mi vieja**. **Al parecer** and **supuestamente** keep a distance from what you''re passing on.', 'draft'),
  ('80763ab8-308e-5552-b59a-ee146b7a8cef', 'd7836b8d-78b8-51ae-8e41-57e6f2d5de34', '¿Está confirmado?', 'A **rumor** is just that until someone **confirma**: *el club confirmó la noticia*. Or as porteños say about any rumour: **dicen que…**', 'draft'),
  ('3aedcd83-cbf5-5910-98dc-1008087f4635', '7768d3dd-52a9-55e1-be73-c2b2153fdb64', 'Me robaron', '**Me robaron el celu** — *my phone got stolen*, literally *they stole the phone from me*. The thief is a **chorro** in lunfardo, a **ladrón** in the news.', 'draft'),
  ('65cb8068-013d-5a1a-b19f-d0c054438a29', '7768d3dd-52a9-55e1-be73-c2b2153fdb64', 'La denuncia', 'To report it you **hacés la denuncia** at the **comisaría**, or online. The **policía** rarely finds the phone; the denuncia is for the insurance and the new SIM.', 'draft'),
  ('91a5e921-8540-53dc-904c-1b0a1d6a8502', '0549fd4c-6be5-5e51-a1f6-4520eabebe83', 'Las expensas', 'Living in a building means paying **expensas** — *the monthly building fees* — to the **consorcio**. The **encargado** is the building''s super, and knows everything.', 'draft'),
  ('d6e4060c-fafa-577a-a626-8cd85c56ee4c', '0549fd4c-6be5-5e51-a1f6-4520eabebe83', 'El calefón', 'The **calefón** heats the water, and breaks in July. When there''s a **pérdida** — *a leak* — you call the **plomero** to **arreglar** it.', 'draft'),
  ('84491d82-9e35-581d-8106-2cc1028f2cde', 'b11e93f9-0410-5c63-9d47-ce8b7e4ebfb9', 'Según, al parecer', '**Según el diario**, **al parecer**, **supuestamente** — passing it on without vouching for it.', 'draft'),
  ('5f1f310a-3dc0-508a-82af-1ac76dfc7a59', 'b11e93f9-0410-5c63-9d47-ce8b7e4ebfb9', 'Me robaron, se rompió', '**Me robaron el celu**, **se rompió el calefón** — and who to call for each.', 'draft'),
  ('bb6b163b-1fc3-54dd-91e3-016a0d3e09ba', '78c71bbd-ead2-54c0-8b92-98f45101f849', '¿De qué cuadro sos?', 'The first question in a new friendship. A club is a **cuadro**, and you don''t choose it, you inherit it: **soy de Boca**, **soy de River**, **hincho por Racing**.', 'draft'),
  ('8f4c23b2-5684-59ec-a311-4cb9e59ce5a6', '78c71bbd-ead2-54c0-8b92-98f45101f849', 'El superclásico', 'Boca against River is **el superclásico**. Any derby is a **clásico**. The fans stand on the **tribuna**.', 'draft'),
  ('1b8d8876-164f-505f-a992-fd2a7dad8f99', 'b612f887-6567-5b36-b3d8-71b680908d0e', 'Gardel cada día canta mejor', 'Carlos **Gardel** died in 1935, and porteños still say he **canta mejor cada día**. A tango''s **letra** — *lyrics* — is usually about **nostalgia**: the barrio, the mother, the woman who left.', 'draft'),
  ('68d76b4c-6e59-5a81-8fd3-40aebff42c9f', 'b612f887-6567-5b36-b3d8-71b680908d0e', 'La milonga', 'A **milonga** is both a dance hall and a faster cousin of the tango. The instrument that sighs is the **bandoneón**.', 'draft'),
  ('9521c790-bf0b-5537-9298-425b9e6009f7', 'ccf7b1e1-a499-5013-99b2-4830d04fca71', 'El asado', 'An asado comes in order: first **chorizo** and **morcilla**, the **achuras**, then the cuts — **vacío**, bife. A **choripán** is a chorizo in bread, the food of every stadium.', 'draft'),
  ('95e185c4-bc0b-5a6f-aaf0-369094e37060', 'ccf7b1e1-a499-5013-99b2-4830d04fca71', '¿Cómo la querés?', 'Meat comes **jugosa** — *pink, juicy* — **a punto** — *medium* — or well done. The **parrilla** is both the grill and the restaurant.', 'draft'),
  ('15e39cea-eee9-586b-a3c7-271f2e64edd6', 'edefc2b5-24ef-5037-9435-816e34d18aaa', 'El cuadro', '**¿De qué cuadro sos?** — and the answer is for life.', 'draft'),
  ('96e2ce80-9484-5837-b645-a03a818d9643', 'edefc2b5-24ef-5037-9435-816e34d18aaa', 'Tango y parrilla', '**Gardel canta mejor cada día**; the meat comes **jugosa** or **a punto**.', 'draft'),
  ('a15090b1-c1fe-5229-a963-37485274bc8d', 'e5014ed4-167a-55b0-8e66-43bd2ee4e434', 'Lo bueno, lo malo', '**Lo** + adjective is *the … thing*: **lo bueno** — *the good thing*; **lo malo** — *the bad thing*; **lo mejor** and **lo peor**. **Lo bueno de vivir acá es que…**', 'draft'),
  ('f9ad308f-67d1-5933-a71a-44ccbfaacf9a', 'e5014ed4-167a-55b0-8e66-43bd2ee4e434', 'No hay nada como…', '**No hay nada como** — *there''s nothing like*: **no hay nada como un asado con amigos**.', 'draft'),
  ('e4442fba-2d7d-515f-bf95-5182892f4c7e', '74a94584-d79a-55af-920c-e6fa1c59b5ad', 'No es que…', 'A reason you deny takes the subjunctive: **no es que no quiera** — *it''s not that I don''t want to*. The real reason follows with **es que** and the normal verb: **es que no puedo**.', 'draft'),
  ('1d62d696-8f13-5ebd-932a-c477849a8b15', '74a94584-d79a-55af-920c-e6fa1c59b5ad', 'Es que…', 'On its own, **es que…** is the start of every porteño excuse: **¿no venís? — Es que laburo temprano**. **El hecho de que** — *the fact that* — is its formal cousin.', 'draft'),
  ('a0157ee6-1047-52d7-bc9d-1f2a42b1f1d5', 'd1ef9d43-816d-571d-a8ba-4ba76a09ba2d', 'Then and now', 'A past that went differently, and what it would mean today: **si hubiera ahorrado** (then), **ahora tendría un depto** (now). The first half is *hubiera* + participle, the second the plain conditional.', 'draft'),
  ('fdea7949-7c65-5ef1-92db-aafc9dc74362', 'd1ef9d43-816d-571d-a8ba-4ba76a09ba2d', 'Hubiéramos', 'With *we*: **si hubiéramos salido antes, ya estaríamos ahí**. The participles: **ahorrado, comprado, vendido, aceptado**.', 'draft'),
  ('f86d96a4-a9c6-57ee-ba1e-65f214cb6352', 'f925644a-c585-5773-8af3-f9a36c4cd2b0', 'Tendría que haber…', '**Tendría que haber** + participle is *I should have*: **tendría que haber ido**, **tendrías que haber avisado**. Porteños use it far more than any other past regret.', 'draft'),
  ('8a29fec5-b96f-5019-8de7-6e3c598a5302', 'f925644a-c585-5773-8af3-f9a36c4cd2b0', 'Me arrepiento', '**Me arrepiento** — *I regret it*; **me arrepentí** — *I regretted it, I changed my mind*. A missed chance is a **oportunidad** you didn''t **aprovechar**.', 'draft'),
  ('b7616641-58f0-580f-9dfb-573e381cdbf5', '8391605b-e3f5-521c-811d-c849d7eef95f', 'No es que…, es que…', '**No es que no quiera** (subjunctive), **es que no puedo** (normal verb).', 'draft'),
  ('9d0bef1d-0d2f-5894-a977-0ce946311b82', '8391605b-e3f5-521c-811d-c849d7eef95f', 'Hubiera, tendría que haber', '**Si hubiera ahorrado, ahora tendría…** — and the regret: **tendría que haber ahorrado**.', 'draft'),
  ('492ceddb-7a1b-5bbd-9bdf-da57d4115735', '35edaab3-b8c0-58db-8415-f52edb278a7e', '-ito, -ita', '**-ito** makes things small, and requests smaller: **un ratito** — *a sec*; **un cafecito**; **un poquito**. It sounds kind rather than childish.', 'draft'),
  ('9c22a7d9-d890-5e17-a088-75954c74be37', '35edaab3-b8c0-58db-8415-f52edb278a7e', 'Cerquita, despacito', 'It works on adverbs too: **cerquita** — *really close*; **despacito** — *nice and slow*. **Chiquito** — *tiny*.', 'draft'),
  ('49e04ee1-475c-5da9-8fc8-72277c9ebf70', '1a2a791f-b759-5930-8cdd-2829e879ce31', 'Lo que pasa es que…', '**Lo que pasa es que…** — *the thing is* — explains the real reason. **Lo raro es que…** — *the weird thing is*; **lo importante es que…** — *what matters is*.', 'draft'),
  ('c6fee335-6750-566b-8494-37dd8682218f', '1a2a791f-b759-5930-8cdd-2829e879ce31', 'Lo de…', '**Lo de** is *the business with*: **¿qué pasó con lo de Juan?** And **lo de siempre** is *the usual*: at the café, at the bar, in life.', 'draft'),
  ('f3b9bf7b-1ef2-5454-ad89-23929822b1a5', '4023fc2a-56e8-5980-bada-adc3306da091', 'Como dice el dicho', 'A **dicho** is a saying, and porteños drop one to close an argument: **más vale tarde que nunca**; **no hay mal que por bien no venga** — *every cloud has a silver lining*.', 'draft'),
  ('e6b7166a-1ef7-5de5-90cc-d87a7c023771', '4023fc2a-56e8-5980-bada-adc3306da091', 'El que avisa no traiciona', '**El que avisa no traiciona** — *I warned you*, literally *who warns doesn''t betray*. **Al mal tiempo, buena cara** — *grin and bear it*.', 'draft'),
  ('c43af633-eebf-5b04-9acd-9b0dcbf2665e', '5ee78c4c-97f9-5e3c-a458-2aff27520c2e', 'Un ratito', '**-ito** softens: **un ratito**, **un cafecito**, **cerquita**.', 'draft'),
  ('cfa102b3-c403-5aec-8b97-167bf132fdf4', '5ee78c4c-97f9-5e3c-a458-2aff27520c2e', 'Lo que pasa es que…', '**Lo que pasa es que**, **lo raro es que**, **lo de siempre** — and a **dicho** to close it.', 'draft'),
  ('c3c9a208-0a25-593c-a6a9-959dfc978b81', 'e0efacaf-93a3-521c-850d-fda4909c6796', 'Chabón, mina', 'A **chabón** is a guy, a **mina** a woman — among friends; both sound rude to strangers. Someone great at what they do is a **groso**; a **birra** is a beer.', 'draft'),
  ('18957af7-bb3a-5323-bc5e-df1ed71877d6', 'e0efacaf-93a3-521c-850d-fda4909c6796', 'Trucho, zarpado', '**Trucho** — *fake, dodgy*: *un billete trucho*. **Zarpado** — *over the top*, for good or bad. **Bardo** — *a mess, trouble*: *se armó un bardo*.', 'draft'),
  ('143b5937-a4e7-5a2c-9851-57ac5a5d2ab1', '24efab50-024b-519e-9029-d2d7f4a05a09', 'Me hizo reír', '**Hacer** + infinitive is *to make someone do*: **me hizo reír**, **me hizo llorar**, **nos hizo esperar**. **Me hace acordar** — *it reminds me*: *esta canción me hace acordar a vos*.', 'draft'),
  ('8845c3ad-88ce-52bb-b23a-7f37ca96a528', '24efab50-024b-519e-9029-d2d7f4a05a09', 'Me reí', '**Reírse** is *to laugh*: **me reí un montón**, **nos reímos de todo**. **Llorar** is *to cry*: **lloré con la película**.', 'draft'),
  ('a1744e6e-5f64-51bf-91b7-8a8dcc1e82f4', '1c04f11a-4feb-5b1d-956b-3661bab59c15', 'Cuanto más…', '**Cuanto más** — *the more*: **cuanto más practicás, mejor hablás**. **Cuanto menos** — *the less*. And **cuanto antes** — *the sooner the better*: **avisame cuanto antes**.', 'draft'),
  ('567d546f-113a-5c05-b6d2-d7f871ea4e89', '1c04f11a-4feb-5b1d-956b-3661bab59c15', 'A medida que', '**A medida que** — *as*, for two things changing together: **a medida que pasa el tiempo, te vas acostumbrando**.', 'draft'),
  ('b5aa4be9-40fc-515c-b131-f7ba25d4134b', '544808fd-b59f-580e-b0be-6f789ba2a11c', 'Chabón, groso', '**Chabón**, **mina**, **groso**, **birra**, **trucho** — among friends.', 'draft'),
  ('bf272180-c68b-56ad-ad51-6be8a4ee5be3', '544808fd-b59f-580e-b0be-6f789ba2a11c', 'Me hizo reír, cuanto más', '**Me hizo reír**, **me hace acordar**, and **cuanto más practicás, mejor**.', 'draft'),
  ('6469f3d2-2cb7-514b-a1e3-9a70a13abe02', '58c98ce0-5227-5f11-bf08-49d656a7808b', 'No te lo tomes a mal', 'Before the hard thing: **no te lo tomes a mal** — *don''t take it the wrong way*; **con todo respeto** — *with all due respect*. After it: **no lo dije para ofenderte**.', 'draft'),
  ('15d2f5ec-cdc6-5240-9c21-970a29b061f5', '58c98ce0-5227-5f11-bf08-49d656a7808b', 'Entre nos', '**Entre nos** — *between you and me* — is where porteño gossip starts. **Sin querer** — *by accident*: **te pisé sin querer**.', 'draft'),
  ('edaaa395-e0c8-5b08-b850-632811be4319', 'e3884c35-d0b6-5d6d-9e7f-b4b1308c5981', 'El plazo', 'At work, a **proyecto** has a **plazo** — *a deadline* — and a **presupuesto** — *a budget*. You **entregás** it to the **cliente**, ideally before you''re **atrasado**.', 'draft'),
  ('4e18b4f7-e094-5c06-b878-27a365a546ec', 'e3884c35-d0b6-5d6d-9e7f-b4b1308c5981', 'Estamos atrasados', '**Estamos atrasados** — *we''re behind*. The porteño answer: **no pasa nada, lo sacamos**.', 'draft'),
  ('5c756d59-7cd0-5412-9357-ac9d9a0882c0', '80d9fccd-c824-5946-8cce-04ecc42e570d', 'Plantear', 'You don''t just ask, you **plantear** it — *raise it, put it on the table*: **le planteé lo del aumento a mi jefa**. Then you **negociar** the **condiciones**.', 'draft'),
  ('8678fb2f-5583-5729-a7fa-7e1ea3ce583d', '80d9fccd-c824-5946-8cce-04ecc42e570d', 'Merezco', '**Merecer** — *to deserve*: **merezco un aumento**, **te lo merecés**. And a boss who **valora** your work says so with the sueldo.', 'draft'),
  ('c4afb4c4-3d89-5295-aca0-b2a95d8259c6', 'f1fe8414-a662-5131-9e76-a258572724ea', 'Me cayó la ficha', '**Me cayó la ficha** — *the penny dropped* — comes from the old phone tokens that fell when the call went through. **Recién ahora me cayó la ficha** — *it only just sank in*.', 'draft'),
  ('6b55c1f4-870b-5f43-8afa-9decf186dca1', 'f1fe8414-a662-5131-9e76-a258572724ea', 'Me da cosa', '**Me da cosa** — *it makes me uneasy, I don''t feel right about it*. **Me pone mal** — *it gets me down*. **Me quedé con las ganas** — *I missed out, and I still want to*.', 'draft'),
  ('3f8c383a-9dd6-5525-bc09-f9763a857332', '908f70c9-72c3-5244-b3c8-db86021008ed', 'El plazo, el aumento', '**Entregar el proyecto** before the **plazo**; **plantear** the raise you **merecés**.', 'draft'),
  ('f3939291-d0bc-5642-8fb0-6e90c7330f1a', '908f70c9-72c3-5244-b3c8-db86021008ed', 'Me cayó la ficha', '**Me cayó la ficha**, **me da cosa**, **me pone mal** — feelings in porteño.', 'draft'),
  ('1cc4dae8-0517-5072-9c8f-c79966f71cc1', '6d5e1fa5-986d-5b45-a406-035e7c99c15c', 'Recorrer', '**Recorrer** is *to travel around, to go all over*: **recorrimos la Patagonia**. The road is the **ruta** — *la ruta 40* runs the length of the country.', 'draft'),
  ('9e49f9b2-c360-58ed-8bf3-a6eca50326ea', '6d5e1fa5-986d-5b45-a406-035e7c99c15c', 'Glaciares y cataratas', 'In the south, **glaciares**; in the north-east, the **cataratas** of Iguazú; in the north-west, Salta''s **paisaje** of red hills.', 'draft'),
  ('04747eea-0365-5b79-8ecf-9b0b35b85709', '5572cf90-36cf-55e2-824b-80f995d2d968', 'Cebar', 'One person **ceba** — pours the water from the **termo** — and passes the mate around the **ronda**. You drink it all, through the **bombilla**, and hand it back to the one who ceba.', 'draft'),
  ('f33a0f3f-b817-5a9d-b4f4-ef4bbaa8b5fa', '5572cf90-36cf-55e2-824b-80f995d2d968', 'Gracias', 'Saying **gracias** when you hand the mate back means *I''m done*. Say it on the first one and that''s your last.', 'draft'),
  ('a5efa082-ec6d-55de-8585-829fc1b6a047', 'cf4d6a07-a4c5-5761-9bad-5a84df508105', 'Llegaron en barco', 'Most porteños have an **abuelo** or **bisabuelo** who **llegó en barco** from Italy or Spain. That''s why a porteño talks with his hands and eats ñoquis on the 29th.', 'draft'),
  ('16b0f92c-4d73-5f11-82c9-5202ed211fa0', 'cf4d6a07-a4c5-5761-9bad-5a84df508105', 'Otra época', '**Era otra época** — *it was a different time*. The **inmigrantes** of the early 20th century built the city''s **conventillos**, its tango and its accent.', 'draft'),
  ('8b631aa6-0830-528d-88e6-e4c219d3acf8', 'a5e76c4c-fdd3-5652-89d4-4d7a8341eae7', 'Recorrer, cebar', '**Recorrimos la Patagonia**; **¿quién ceba?** — the country and its ritual.', 'draft'),
  ('e27d1543-3b4b-5956-85fa-c4bfef64aba7', 'a5e76c4c-fdd3-5652-89d4-4d7a8341eae7', 'Llegaron en barco', '**Mis abuelos llegaron de Italia en barco** — otra **época**.', 'draft'),
  ('598bffd2-cea9-5528-8b85-1bec66093ce9', 'cc075128-b483-5ba0-a24a-485bd1dc71fa', '¿Me estás cargando?', '**Cargar** someone is *to tease, to wind up*: **¿me estás cargando?** — *are you pulling my leg?* Porteños **cargan** the people they like; being left alone is the bad sign.', 'draft'),
  ('e7590664-dc43-56d6-aa5e-259e9a000d5b', 'cc075128-b483-5ba0-a24a-485bd1dc71fa', 'En joda', '**Lo dije en joda** — *I was joking*. A **chiste** is a joke you tell; if it lands, it''s **gracioso**.', 'draft'),
  ('8a55c90c-0fb5-5815-a6a0-17ca65ce25bc', '35da2974-7119-59d7-bdf3-d14bdf042064', 'Se casó', '**Casarse** is *to get married*: **se casó**, **nos casamos en marzo**. The wedding is a **casamiento**, and porteño ones end at six in the morning.', 'draft'),
  ('72f9a5c3-4b46-54b5-8f98-201dfd121794', '35da2974-7119-59d7-bdf3-d14bdf042064', 'Nació', '**Nacer** — *to be born*: **¿dónde naciste?**, **el bebé nació ayer**. **Está embarazada** — *she''s pregnant*.', 'draft'),
  ('cca2ccce-cf17-599f-8925-4e509a09fbef', 'a25229c0-af37-50d8-86db-83c809276632', 'Me emocioné', '**Emocionarse** is *to be moved, to get emotional* — never just *excited*: **me emocioné en el casamiento**. **Se me puso la piel de gallina** — *I got goosebumps*.', 'draft'),
  ('73a05d53-1c14-5efb-ad11-2e0630cff1d7', 'a25229c0-af37-50d8-86db-83c809276632', 'Orgulloso', '**Estoy orgulloso de vos** — *I''m proud of you*. **Agradecido** — *grateful*: **estoy muy agradecida**.', 'draft'),
  ('5571e01e-7110-522a-bd2f-bed64e49f2b0', 'f6864f2a-0faf-53cf-a8b4-9e35f6661b10', '¿Me estás cargando?', '**Cargar**, **en joda**, **un chiste gracioso** — humour, porteño style.', 'draft'),
  ('65ea12f5-9f24-5b33-96b2-d70a5923a81c', 'f6864f2a-0faf-53cf-a8b4-9e35f6661b10', 'Se casó, nació', '**Se casó**, **nació**, **me emocioné** — the news that matters.', 'draft'),
  ('bb475835-3596-5744-abe5-6a802edce685', 'c1be6404-2a36-51f7-8d0f-43b1a6d26250', 'Lo lograste', '**Lograr** — *to manage, to pull off*: **¡lo lograste!** — *you did it!* **Felicitaciones** is how the course says it; **¡grande!** is how a porteño would.', 'draft'),
  ('8e491aaa-a221-5434-b38f-8e4c46b7a2ea', 'c1be6404-2a36-51f7-8d0f-43b1a6d26250', 'Ya sos de acá', 'When your **acento** gives you away less and less, someone will say **ya sos de acá** — *you''re one of us now*. Take it: it''s the highest praise the city has.', 'draft')
